255:Notifies the client that a session entry was created on the server and will never be sent. This happens under output suppression (see [tool-responses.md](../hal-engine-tool-responses/spec.md)): the server keeps the entry so the model retains context, and the client does not need it for display ([validated by: still records a suppressed reply in the session, so history keeps it](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L247)).
